# Backrest — the keys stored in secrets.sops.json, one value each (`sopsgen
# apply` fills generated ones, `sopsedit` the rest). Values built from other
# secrets live in env.nix. Key set must match secrets.sops.json and
# tests/fixtures/stacks/backrest.sops.json.
# config-init REFUSES to seed config.json while any value still says changeme.

# Restic
# One of the two things between you and permanent data loss (the age key is the
# other), and it is stored encrypted TO that key — keep a copy offline, outside
# this infrastructure, and NOT only in Vaultwarden (whose backup uses it).
# openssl rand -base64 48
RESTIC_PASSWORD='changeme_restic_password_single_quoted'

# Backrest UI
# BASE64 OF the bcrypt hash — backrest base64-decodes before comparing, so a
# raw bcrypt can never log in.
# htpasswd -bnBC 10 "" 'yourpassword' | tr -d ':\n' | base64 -w0
BACKREST_ADMIN_PASSWORD_BCRYPT=changeme_base64_of_bcrypt_hash

# Dead-man switch
# Pinged on every successful fast-volume snapshot. Use a service that alerts on
# the ABSENCE of a ping (healthchecks.io) — it is the only check that catches a
# timer that silently stopped firing.
DEADMAN_URL=https://hc-ping.com/changeme-uuid
